<title>USA: Vitalink Pharmacy completes TeamCare merger.</title>
<headline>Vitalink Pharmacy completes TeamCare merger.</headline>
<dateline>NAPERVILLE, Ill. 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vitalink Pharmacy Services Inc said Thursday it completed its merger with TeamCare, the institutional pharmacy business of GranCare Inc.</p>
<p>Vitalink said it issued about 11.6 million common shares as part of a stock swap deal valued at about $370 million. Vitalink also assumed about $107 million in debt.</p>
<p>The deal makes Vitalink the nation's second-largest publicly traded institutional pharmacy company with annual revenues of more than $420 million, the company said.</p>
<p>Vitalink shares were trading up 1/2 at 24-3/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
